-- title:
--   Kronecker congruence pins j ≡ jₚ^{ p} on the second branch
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $F = \mathbb{Q}\bigl(\{\,q\text{-expansions } j(q^d) : d \mid p\,\}\bigr) \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ be the field `modularFunctionFieldFull p`, with $j =$ `IgusaScheme.jFull p` the element of $F$ given by the Laurent series `jq`. Let $jp$ be an element of the subalgebra of $F$ consisting of elements integral over $\mathbb{Z}[j]$, whose underlying Laurent series is $\mathrm{qExpand}_{\mathbb{Q}}\,p\,(jq)$, i.e. $j(q^p)$. Let $W_0 \neq W_1$ be valuation subrings of $F$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of each, such that for $i = 0,1$ and every $P \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ with $P \bmod p \neq 0$ both $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ lie in $W_i$, and such that every valuation subring $V$ of $F$ with $p$ in its maximal ideal and with this same property for all such $P$ equals $W_0$ or $W_1$. Assume further that $jp - j^{\,p}$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$; that every $x \in W_0$ admits $P, Q \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ with $Q \bmod p \neq 0$ and $x\,Q(j) - P(j)$ in the maximal ideal of $W_0$; and that every $x \in W_1$ admits $P, Q \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ with $Q \bmod p \neq 0$ and $x\,Q(jp) - P(jp)$ in the maximal ideal of $W_1$. Then $j - jp^{\,p}$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_1$.
--
--   This is the branch-by-branch form of Kronecker's congruence $\Phi_p(X,Y) \equiv (X^p - Y)(X - Y^p) \pmod p$: on the branch $W_0$ of the modular curve of level $p$ in characteristic $p$ whose residue field is generated by the reduction of $j$ one has $j_p \equiv j^{\,p}$, and the statement pins the crossed Frobenius relation $j \equiv j_p^{\,p}$ on the other branch $W_1$, whose residue field is generated by the reduction of $j_p$. It feeds the identification of the quotients of the integral chart algebra attached to such a pair of valuation subrings, in [`ModularCurve.DRModel.exists_ringEquiv_quotient_chartAlgFin_polynomial_of_valuationSubring_pair`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModel.exists_ringEquiv_quotient_chartAlgFin_polynomial_of_valuationSubring_pair).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_DRModel_jFull_sub_pow_mem_nonunits_of_valuationSubring_pair.lean

